{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7865585","formula":"C₁₆H₂₇N₅O","hill":"C16H27N5O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":27.0,"N":5.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"UR-AK49"},"descriptions":{"en":"UR-AK49 is a drug used in scientific research which acts as a potent antagonist for the Neuropeptide Y / Pancreatic polypeptide receptor Y4, and also as a partial agonist at the histamine receptors H1 and H2. UR-AK49 is a pure antagonist at Y4 with no partial agonist effects, and although it is only slightly selective for Y4 over the related Y1 and Y5 receptors, as the first non-peptide Y4 antagonist developed UR-AK49 is expected to be useful in the study of this receptor and its role in the body."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":25149433,"mass":305.42,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCC(CC1)CCC(=O)NC(=NCCCC2=CN=CN2)N","inchikey":"QBGKYFYOFBXHFM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-cyclohexyl-N-[N'-[3-(1H-imidazol-5-yl)propyl]carbamimidoyl]propanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"25149433","atoms":49,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.33,"y":0.042,"z":-0.114,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.535,"y":-2.264,"z":0.243,"el":"N"},{"x":1.714,"y":-1.836,"z":-0.108,"el":"N"},{"x":0.939,"y":-4.062,"z":0.31,"el":"N"},{"x":4.626,"y":2.326,"z":0.08,"el":"N"},{"x":6.813,"y":2.284,"z":-0.302,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.593,"y":0.541,"z":0.329,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.083,"y":1.961,"z":0.646,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.278,"y":-0.004,"z":-0.932,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.605,"y":2.021,"z":0.755,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.799,"y":0.06,"z":-0.82,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.281,"y":1.471,"z":-0.496,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.074,"y":0.517,"z":0.171,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.52,"y":-0.898,"z":0.303,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.013,"y":-0.952,"z":0.117,"el":"C"},{"x":0.789,"y":-2.707,"z":0.136,"el":"C"},{"x":4.019,"y":-1.173,"z":-0.556,"el":"C"},{"x":4.025,"y":-0.085,"z":0.523,"el":"C"},{